The frontend is compiled locally from the pinned official source and locked npm
packages, not copied from a third-party website. assets/upstream-manifest.json
records the source archive and generated asset SHA-256 hashes. build-web.py
contains the complete build adaptation: Chrome 111 target, worker virtual-module
plugins, disabled PWA replacement, relative provider API bases, and direct GitHub
codeload URL for the same locked KuGouMusicApi dependency version.
Lightning CSS 1.32.0 lowers hex-alpha colors for legacy Android targetSdk.
compat-assets.mjs uses Babel parser 7.29.9 for embedded color literals.
core-js 3.51.0 (MIT; license in licenses/core-js.txt) supplies newer JS APIs.

Java loopback serving, pointer input, HTTP transport bridge and Android file
selection are nTv adaptations in this directory and app/src/main/java/xiao/bu/tv.
Online music APIs remain external services; no Node.js backend is embedded.
No account credentials or music files are included. The adapter source is
provided under AGPL-3.0 together with this package.

The Android file adapter provides read-only, IndexedDB-persisted copies of files
explicitly selected by the user. The Vite adaptation enables local-library
availability for this bridge. It does not claim desktop directory watching or
write access. Media getAttribute(src) is mapped back to the original URL so the
upstream autoplay source guard agrees with the Java proxy transport.

When no system document Activity is enabled, Android 7-12 can use the bundled
read-only file picker after granting storage read permission. It does not enable
system components or bypass Android's permissions. Newer Android versions need
an enabled system picker if the legacy read permission is unavailable.
